- **Daily signals:** I followed the earlier H-015/H-016 approach: daily candles come in through the 1d informative frame and `merge_informative_pair`, so a day''s value is only used after that day has closed.
- **Entry and exit:** Entry and exit follow the proposal: RSI(2) below 10 with close above the 200-day SMA to enter, and close above the 5-day SMA or below the 200-day SMA to exit. `stoploss` is -0.99, as the proposal specifies.
- **Start-up candles:** `startup_candle_count` is 400, as the proposal says. It relies on Freqtrade loading 400 candles of each timeframe, which the H-016 docstring states and I did not check here. The static strategy check was not run (it is outside the allowed commands), so it may flag this against the 4,500 limit.
- **Entry timing:** The entry flag stays set on every 1h candle of the day after the signal while the condition holds. The engine takes only one position, so that does not stack trades.
- **Test stubs:** The test file''s stubs load before `test_strategy.py`, so they include the SMA and RSI stubs that file defines. Without them, four other tests failed in the full-suite run.','2026-11-04T21:41:04.881618+00:00');

