The rule is implemented as written, with no changes to any number:
- **Signals:** they come from closed daily candles through the `@informative("1d")` merge, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed.
- **Entry and exit:** entry is IBS < 0.2 with daily close above SMA200. Exit is IBS ≥ 0.8 or a daily close below SMA200.
- **Stop:** the 12% stop is `stoploss = -0.12`.
- **Warm-up:** `startup_candle_count` is 400.

A zero-range day (high equals low) has no IBS, so it produces neither entry nor exit. The safety exit is also skipped on such a day, because you said those days give no signal. It fires on the next normal day if the close is still below SMA200.

The signals are level-based, so they are set on every 1h candle of the day after the daily close. Freqtrade handles the "no open position" condition.

I did not test the real Freqtrade merge. The tests emulate it with a backward merge on date plus one day, the same way the H-020 test does.','2026-11-05T18:24:13.541265+00:00');

