INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-001','SmaTrendBaseline','SMA20/SMA50 cross, close > SMA200, stop -10%','2026-10-20T00:00:00Z','BTC/USDT 1h through 2026-10-20','frozen reference','Original result (1 trade) was a harness artifact. Re-tested 2026-11-02 under the corrected harness (exploration, BTC/ETH/BNB): rejected on all three, drawdown 44-50% at base, 74-88% at stress; lookahead and recursive pass.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-002','DonchianBreakoutBaseline','Close > prior 20-candle high; exit below prior 10-candle low; stop -10%','2026-10-20T00:00:00Z','BTC/USDT 1h through 2026-10-20','rejected at exploration','Corrected harness, exploration on BTC/ETH/BNB: positive only at the optimistic cost, drawdown 60-98%. Do not select by return alone.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-003','BollingerMeanReversionBaseline','Lower 20-band, RSI14 < 30, close > SMA200; exit at middle band; stop -10%','2026-10-20T00:00:00Z','BTC/USDT 1h through 2026-10-20','rejected at exploration','Not yet tested under the corrected harness. Trend-failure risk. [Audit 2026-11-04, provisional (gates.json PROPOSED), exploration only: correction: the ''not yet tested'' remark above is outdated. Re-run under the corrected harness 2026-10-30 (exploration): rejected on BTC, ETH and BNB. Base net profit BTC -14.8, ETH -19.9, BNB +48.7; profit factor 0.82/0.72/1.60. Source: research/audit/H-003-exploration-metrics.json. Protected baseline, stays in the strategy path.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-004','SlowTimeSeriesMomentum','Use closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole balance. ENTRY: close > highest high of the prior 1440 bars (60 days, excluding current bar) AND close > SMA(4800 bars, 200 days) of close AND no open position. EXIT: close < lowest low of the prior 720 bars (30 days, excluding current bar), OR close below entry price by 15% (hard stop, checked on closed bars). After any exit, no re-entry until at least 168 bars (7 days) have passed. No other filters, no pyramiding, no take-profit.','2026-10-30T13:28:34.345485+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h through 2026-10-30; no result data viewed beyond the context file''s exploration summaries','invalid: implementation deviated from rule','Exploration ran on an implementation that used min_periods=1440 on the 4800-candle SMA (to satisfy a too-short smoke window) and without the 168-candle cooldown (backtest ran without --enable-protections). Both harness flaws are fixed. The rule itself is untested. Recorded results: research/experiments/H-004-exploration/ and the 20261030T133614Z-h-004-* manifests. Strategy file removed 2026-11-03 (implementation flawed; the 4800-bar SMA exceeds the loadable warm-up). Recoverable from git history (commit 544a3d5). [Audit 2026-11-04, provisional (gates.json PROPOSED), exploration only: classified invalid (rule untested). File removed from the strategy path without going to _archive/; documented exception, recoverable from git 544a3d5.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-005','VolatilitySqueezeBreakout','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole balance. Definitions (all use completed bars): R(t) = (highest high of the 168 bars ending at t - lowest low of the 168 bars ending at t) / close(t). Squeeze(t) is true if R(t) is <= the 20th percentile of R over the 2160 bars ending at t-1 (rolling quantile 0.20, excluding the current bar). ENTRY at close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) Squeeze was true on at least one of the previous 24 bars (t-24..t-1); (2) close(t) > highest high of the prior 168 bars (t-168..t-1, excluding current bar); (3) close(t) > SMA(2400) of close; (4) no open position; (5) cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t when close(t) < lowest low of the prior 336 bars (t-336..t-1, excluding current), or via the hard stop. STOP-LOSS: fixed 8% below entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 72 candles after any exit. No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 2400 bars.','2026-10-30T13:49:38.324198+00:00','No price data viewed; only the context file and validation protocol (BTC, ETH, BNB 1h description through 2026-10-30).','rejected at exploration','Long breakout after a multi-day volatility squeeze in an established uptrend');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-006','RegimeGatedPullbackTrend','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole balance. REGIME at bar t (all must hold): (a) close(t) > SMA(4800) of close; (b) SMA(2400)(t) > SMA(4800)(t); (c) SMA(4800)(t) > SMA(4800)(t-720). ENTRY at close of bar t when REGIME holds AND min(close over bars t-48..t-1) <= 0.95 * max(high over bars t-336..t-1) (a pullback of at least 5% from the 14-day high occurred within the last 48 bars) AND close(t) > SMA(48) of close AND close(t-1) <= SMA(48) at t-1 (fresh recovery cross above the 2-day mean) AND no open position AND cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t (executed next open) when any of: close(t) >= max(high over bars t-336..t-1) (prior 14-day high retested); close(t) < SMA(4800)(t) (regime lost); 240 bars have elapsed since entry (time stop). STOP-LOSS: fixed 5% below entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 48 candles after any exit. No pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 5520 bars.','2026-10-30T17:42:27.332302+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h through 2026-10-20; exploration results listed in the context file only','failed','Bull-regime-only pullback re-entry with long-term slope gate and tight fixed stop Strategy file removed 2026-11-03 (never ran: warm-up 5520 > 4500). Idea re-implemented as H-010. Recoverable from git history (commit 544a3d5). [Audit 2026-11-04, provisional (gates.json PROPOSED), exploration only: classified invalid (never ran). File removed without going to _archive/; documented exception, recoverable from git 544a3d5.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-007','RisingTrendBreakoutGate','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole balance. REGIME at bar t (all must hold): (a) SMA(1200)(t) > SMA(2400)(t); (b) SMA(2400)(t) > SMA(2400)(t-480) (long mean rising over the last 20 days); (c) close(t) > SMA(1200)(t). ENTRY at close of bar t when REGIME holds AND close(t) > highest high of the prior 480 bars (t-480..t-1, excluding current bar) AND no open position AND cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t (executed next open) when close(t) < lowest low of the prior 240 bars (t-240..t-1, excluding current bar) OR close(t) < SMA(1200)(t) (regime lost). STOP-LOSS: fixed 6% below entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 120 candles after any exit. No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 2880 bars (SMA(2400) plus 480-bar slope lag); startup_candle_count should be set to 2880 or a bit more (at most 4500) so recursive analysis is stable.','2026-10-30T18:29:04.404068+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h exploration-period summary results listed in the context file only, through 2026-10-30; no validation results seen','rejected at exploration','20-day breakout only inside a confirmed, rising multi-month uptrend, with 10-day channel exit [2026-11-03 step 0.3: has_bias on BNB traced to an 11 h data gap at 2019-05-15 03:00-12:00 plus analyzer truncation, not to the code; see research/h007-bnb-lookahead-2026-11-03.md. Decision unchanged.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-008','VolatilitySqueezeBreakout','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole balance. Definitions (all use completed bars): R(t) = (highest high of the 168 bars ending at t - lowest low of the 168 bars ending at t) / close(t). Squeeze(t) is true if R(t) is <= the 20th percentile of R over the 2160 bars ending at t-1 (rolling quantile 0.20, excluding the current bar). ENTRY at close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) Squeeze was true on at least one of the previous 24 bars (t-24..t-1); (2) close(t) > highest high of the prior 168 bars (t-168..t-1, excluding current bar); (3) close(t) > SMA(2400) of close; (4) no open position; (5) cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t when close(t) < lowest low of the prior 336 bars (t-336..t-1, excluding current), or via the hard stop. STOP-LOSS: fixed 8% below entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 72 candles after any exit. No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 2400 bars. EXPOSURE (the only change from H-005): each trade uses 20% of the account (tradable_balance_ratio 0.20), the rest stays in cash. Rule for the number: the largest exposure on a 5% grid for which the seeded block-bootstrap (lab/bootstrap.py, block 3, 4000 resamples, seed 1) 95th-percentile closed-trade max drawdown of the H-005 exploration trades is <= 25% on BTC, ETH and BNB at once; that gives 20% (p95 20%/22%/24%; 25% gives 24%/27%/29%). Only exploration trades were used; the validation split and the final test were not read.','2026-11-02T23:39:49.008873+00:00','H-005 exploration trade lists and metrics (BTC, ETH, BNB) through 2026-10-30; no validation or final-test results seen.','not approved at validation','Exploration: candidate on BTC/ETH/BNB (drawdown 12-14%). Validation (read once, 2024-07..2026-10): profit positive on all three (+6.3/+6.9/+10.3 on 100) with drawdown 2.4-7.7%, but only 12/10/8 trades (gate needs 30, so inconclusive) and profit without the best trade negative on BTC and BNB. Not a candidate. [Audit 2026-11-04, provisional (gates.json PROPOSED), exploration only: IS->OOS base profit per day: BTC -76%, ETH -76%, BNB -82%. Exploration max drawdown on closed trades 10-13%, mark-to-market 20-30%. Source: research/audit/fase2-diagnostico.md.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-009','WeeklyBreakoutRegime','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance. REGIME at bar t: SMA(720)(t) > SMA(2160)(t) AND close(t) > SMA(720)(t). ENTRY at close of bar t when REGIME holds AND close(t) > highest high of the prior 168 bars (t-168..t-1, excluding current bar) AND no open position AND cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t (executed next open) when close(t) < lowest low of the prior 72 bars (excluding current bar) OR close(t) < SMA(720)(t). STOP-LOSS: fixed 6% below entry (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: 24 candles after any exit. No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 2160 bars. EXPOSURE: each trade uses a fixed share of the account (tradable_balance_ratio), the rest stays in cash. The share is the largest value on a 5% grid for which the seeded block-bootstrap (lab/bootstrap.py choose_exposure: block 3, 4000 resamples, seed 1) 95th-percentile closed-trade max drawdown is <= 25% on BTC, ETH and BNB at once, computed from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost with full exposure (a calibration run, exploration split only). The value is recorded in the notes after calibration; the rule for choosing it is fixed now. If the calibration run shows fewer than 30 trades on any pair the hypothesis is dropped, not retuned. Validation split and final test not read.','2026-11-02T23:59:40.709384+00:00','Context summaries plus H-005/H-007/H-008 results and general literature (tradingstrategy.ai learn pages: Donchian/trend and moving-average timing); no result of this rule seen.','candidate at exploration','7-day breakout in a 30d/90d uptrend: more trades per year than H-007 (20-day breakout), regime gate shortened to match. Textbook horizons, no tuning. Calibrated exposure: 0.25 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.11619927151132928, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.2167829050039351, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.23302999449418582}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 58, ''ETH/USDT'': 81, ''BNB/USDT'': 80}. [Audit 2026-11-04, provisional (gates.json PROPOSED), exploration only: classified candidate at exploration; validation NOT read. Reviewers: no lookahead or fidelity error. Caveats: largest BNB trade = 80% of profit; bootstrap 95% CI of total return includes 0 on ETH and BNB; base_2x Sharpe beats buy-and-hold and Sma200Baseline (same exposure) on BTC only; daily correlation with Sma200Baseline 0.71 on BNB; mark-to-market drawdown 11%/25%/32% vs gate 7.2%/18.5%/14.5%. research/proposals/H-009.json does not exist. Source: research/audit/H-009-exploration-metrics.json.] [Frozen for dry-run evidence collection 2026-11-04T21:39:32.190375+00:00, commit c48de4fff8, strategy sha256 c6baa8220d58; Dry-run como coleta de evidência: NÃO validada; sem evidência prospectiva; não é aprovação, não é holdout e não consome a leitura da validação.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-010','UptrendPullbackRecovery','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance. REGIME at bar t: close(t) > SMA(2400)(t) AND SMA(720)(t) > SMA(2400)(t). ENTRY at close of bar t when REGIME holds AND min(close over bars t-48..t-1) <= 0.95 * max(high over bars t-336..t-1) (a pullback of at least 5% from the 14-day high within the last 48 bars) AND close(t) > SMA(48)(t) AND close(t-1) <= SMA(48)(t-1) (fresh recovery cross) AND no open position AND cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t (executed next open) when close(t) >= max(high over bars t-336..t-1) OR close(t) < SMA(2400)(t). STOP-LOSS: fixed 5% below entry (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: 48 candles after any exit. No time stop, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 2400 bars. EXPOSURE: each trade uses a fixed share of the account (tradable_balance_ratio), the rest stays in cash. The share is the largest value on a 5% grid for which the seeded block-bootstrap (lab/bootstrap.py choose_exposure: block 3, 4000 resamples, seed 1) 95th-percentile closed-trade max drawdown is <= 25% on BTC, ETH and BNB at once, computed from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost with full exposure (a calibration run, exploration split only). The value is recorded in the notes after calibration; the rule for choosing it is fixed now. If the calibration run shows fewer than 30 trades on any pair the hypothesis is dropped, not retuned. Validation split and final test not read.','2026-11-02T23:59:40.709384+00:00','Context summaries plus H-005/H-007/H-008 results and general literature (tradingstrategy.ai learn pages: Donchian/trend and moving-average timing); no result of this rule seen.','rejected at exploration','H-006 idea (never ran: 5520-bar warm-up) with a 2400-bar long mean so it fits the 4500 limit; no time stop. Untested before. Calibrated exposure: 0.10 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.17472074793385642, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.24208648328033058, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.20134252321239815}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 145, ''ETH/USDT'': 187, ''BNB/USDT'': 173}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-011','TripleBottomReversal','Closed candles only; signal at candle close, order at next open. Long only, one position, no averaging down. Pivot low at i = lowest low of [i-5,i+5] (ties allowed on the left only), KNOWN only at the close of candle i+5. Three consecutive pivot lows L1,L2,L3 (i1<i2<i3) form the support zone if (max L - min L)/mean L <= 2%, consecutive bottoms >= 12 candles apart, i3-i1 <= 150 candles. Recoveries: H1 = highest high in (i1,i2), H2 = highest high in (i2,i3); both must be >= mean bottom * 1.03. Neckline = max(H1,H2). ENTRY at the first close above the neckline at t in [i3+5, i3+5+30] and before a fourth pivot is confirmed, if no earlier close since i3 was above it, no low since i3 is below min bottom * 0.98, volume(t) >= mean volume of the previous 20 candles. Optional filters OFF in the tested rule: RSI14 higher at i3 than at i1 (positive divergence), close > EMA200. STOP at min bottom - 0.5*ATR14(t) (fixed at entry, via custom_stoploss from the signal candle). TARGET neckline + 1.0*(neckline - mean bottom). TIME STOP 150 candles. Min R/R filter configurable, OFF (0.0) because stop below support and entry at the neckline make R/R < 1 by construction. A pattern signals once and a later pattern must start after the previous signalled pattern''s last bottom (no duplicate entries). Warm-up: 800 bars. EXPOSURE: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, computed from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; calibration run; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Validation and final test not read. Parameters are textbook values fixed before any result.','2026-11-03T14:11:52.700407+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h and 4h candles through 2026-10-30 (4h downloaded 2026-11-03); results of H-001..H-010 known, including the one-time validation read of H-008 (a different rule on the same 2024-07..2026-10 window) - the validation split is therefore not blind for this family of ideas. No result of THIS rule seen.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Triple bottom reversal, 1h. User-requested; reversal pattern, structurally R/R<1. DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 9, ''ETH/USDT'': 5, ''BNB/USDT'': 6} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-012','EMASnapbackATR','Closed candles only; signal at candle close, order at next open. Long only, one position, no DCA, no martingale. z(t) = (close - EMA20)/ATR14. STRETCH: min z over the previous 6 candles (t-6..t-1) <= -2.0. ENTRY at close of t when stretch AND close(t) > EMA200(t) AND close(t) > high(t-1) (recovery confirmation) AND close(t) < EMA20(t) AND no open position AND cooldown. Optional RSI (min RSI14 over the lookback <= 35) and volume (>= mean of previous 20 candles) filters are OFF in the tested rule. STOP close(t) - 2.0*ATR14(t), fixed at entry. EXIT first close >= EMA20 (executed next open); time stop after 48 candles; alternative exit ''rr'' (1.5R target) exists as a documented option and is only an ablation. COOLDOWN 6 candles after any exit. Warm-up: 800 bars. EXPOSURE: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Validation and final test not read. Parameters are textbook values fixed before any result.','2026-11-03T14:11:52.708727+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h and 4h candles through 2026-10-30 (4h downloaded 2026-11-03); results of H-001..H-010 known, including the one-time validation read of H-008 (a different rule on the same 2024-07..2026-10 window) - the validation split is therefore not blind for this family of ideas. No result of THIS rule seen.','rejected at exploration','EMA20 ATR-normalised snapback inside an EMA200 uptrend, 1h. User-requested; mean reversion, a family that failed before (H-003). Calibrated exposure: 0.2 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.14187785490232907, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.18023420143817828, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.22869875887657765}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 121, ''ETH/USDT'': 114, ''BNB/USDT'': 129}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-013','TripleBottomReversal','Closed candles only; signal at candle close, order at next open. Long only, one position, no averaging down. Pivot low at i = lowest low of [i-5,i+5] (ties allowed on the left only), KNOWN only at the close of candle i+5. Three consecutive pivot lows L1,L2,L3 (i1<i2<i3) form the support zone if (max L - min L)/mean L <= 2%, consecutive bottoms >= 12 candles apart, i3-i1 <= 150 candles. Recoveries: H1 = highest high in (i1,i2), H2 = highest high in (i2,i3); both must be >= mean bottom * 1.03. Neckline = max(H1,H2). ENTRY at the first close above the neckline at t in [i3+5, i3+5+30] and before a fourth pivot is confirmed, if no earlier close since i3 was above it, no low since i3 is below min bottom * 0.98, volume(t) >= mean volume of the previous 20 candles. Optional filters OFF in the tested rule: RSI14 higher at i3 than at i1 (positive divergence), close > EMA200. STOP at min bottom - 0.5*ATR14(t) (fixed at entry, via custom_stoploss from the signal candle). TARGET neckline + 1.0*(neckline - mean bottom). TIME STOP 150 candles. Min R/R filter configurable, OFF (0.0) because stop below support and entry at the neckline make R/R < 1 by construction. A pattern signals once and a later pattern must start after the previous signalled pattern''s last bottom (no duplicate entries). Timeframe 4h, same constants in candles. Warm-up: 800 bars. EXPOSURE: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, computed from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; calibration run; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Validation and final test not read. Parameters are textbook values fixed before any result.','2026-11-03T14:11:52.712481+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h and 4h candles through 2026-10-30 (4h downloaded 2026-11-03); results of H-001..H-010 known, including the one-time validation read of H-008 (a different rule on the same 2024-07..2026-10 window) - the validation split is therefore not blind for this family of ideas. No result of THIS rule seen.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Same rule as H-011 on 4h candles (counts as a variant of the family). DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 5, ''ETH/USDT'': 3, ''BNB/USDT'': 1} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-014','EMASnapbackATR','Closed candles only; signal at candle close, order at next open. Long only, one position, no DCA, no martingale. z(t) = (close - EMA20)/ATR14. STRETCH: min z over the previous 6 candles (t-6..t-1) <= -2.0. ENTRY at close of t when stretch AND close(t) > EMA200(t) AND close(t) > high(t-1) (recovery confirmation) AND close(t) < EMA20(t) AND no open position AND cooldown. Optional RSI (min RSI14 over the lookback <= 35) and volume (>= mean of previous 20 candles) filters are OFF in the tested rule. STOP close(t) - 2.0*ATR14(t), fixed at entry. EXIT first close >= EMA20 (executed next open); time stop after 48 candles; alternative exit ''rr'' (1.5R target) exists as a documented option and is only an ablation. COOLDOWN 6 candles after any exit. Timeframe 4h, same constants in candles. Warm-up: 800 bars. EXPOSURE: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Validation and final test not read. Parameters are textbook values fixed before any result.','2026-11-03T14:11:52.715708+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h and 4h candles through 2026-10-30 (4h downloaded 2026-11-03); results of H-001..H-010 known, including the one-time validation read of H-008 (a different rule on the same 2024-07..2026-10 window) - the validation split is therefore not blind for this family of ideas. No result of THIS rule seen.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Same rule as H-012 on 4h candles (counts as a variant of the family). DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 33, ''ETH/USDT'': 27, ''BNB/USDT'': 32} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-015','TimeSeriesMomentum','Closed DAILY candles (Freqtrade informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair), executed on 1h at the next open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance, no stop-loss, no sizing hooks. mom(d) = close(d)/close(d-N days) - 1. ENTRY while mom > 0 (and, with the regime, regime_on() true = daily close > SMA(200); vol_regime off per the step-1.4 ablation). EXIT when mom <= 0 (or the regime turns off). GRID (pre-declared, complete): N in {30, 60, 90, 120, 180} x regime in {off, on} = 10 configurations; N_trials for the DSR = 10. Each configuration is also a test at costs base and base_2x on each of BTC, ETH, BNB. Warm-up 400 bars (daily and 1h). PASS CRITERIA TO READ VALIDATION (fixed before running, all required): DSR of the best configuration (N=10) >= 0.95; PBO (CSCV, 16 slices) <= 0.5; plateau (neighbouring N with the same regime flag reach >= 70% of the best Sharpe); Sharpe above buy-and-hold AND above Sma200Baseline at base_2x in the IS; >= 30 trades per pair; lab/config/gates.json clear on exploration. Fail = family rejected and archived. The validation split is then read ONCE, for the configuration chosen in the IS. Final test / prospective holdout not read.','2026-11-04T00:11:34.975802+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h/4h/1d candles through 2026-11-02; results of H-001..H-014 known, including the one-time validation read of H-008 and the Sma200Baseline cycle table (so the validation window is not blind for trend-following ideas). No result of THIS rule seen. Regime-filter ablation (IS only) known.','rejected (family): configuration H-016 not approved at validation','Step 2, family 1 of 3 (TSMOM). Pre-registered grid of 10; textbook horizons. [2026-11-03 grid explored on the IS (research/grids/H-015-exploration.json): best N30_noreg; DSR 0.999, PBO 0.31, plateau pass, beats B&H and Sma200 at base_2x, >= 89 trades per pair; selected cell registered as H-016.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-016','TimeSeriesMomentum','Same rule as H-015 with N_DAYS = 30 and no regime filter (the H-015 grid winner at base_2x in the exploration split: pooled Sharpe 1.49 vs buy-and-hold 1.15 and Sma200Baseline 1.05; DSR(N=10) 0.999; PBO 0.31; plateau 0.83 of the best at N=60). Closed daily candles via merge_informative_pair, executed on 1h at the next open; long only, one position, no stop-loss, no sizing hooks. ENTRY while close(d)/close(d-30) > 1; EXIT when it is <= 1. N_trials inherited from H-015 = 10 (this is not a new draw: it is the selected cell of that grid; the family counts 11 registered hypotheses). Exposure: fixed share chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure). Gates of lab/config/gates.json on exploration; only if all clear, the validation split is read ONCE. Final test / prospective holdout not read.','2026-11-04T00:34:35.725730+00:00','Same as H-015 plus the full exploration grid of H-015 (which is where this configuration was chosen). The validation split has not been read for this rule; it was read once for H-008 (a different rule).','not approved at validation','Child of H-015. Winner at the grid edge (N=30, the shortest horizon): the plateau test has one neighbour only. Calibrated exposure: 0.15 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.19407518252890127, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.15886218231018612, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.20444195374091295}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 94, ''ETH/USDT'': 89, ''BNB/USDT'': 96}. [Validation read once (exposure 0.15): BTC rejected (profit ex-best trade -5.2), ETH candidate, BNB rejected (ex-best -3.2). Report: research/grids/H-015-report.md. Code archived.] [Audit 2026-11-04, provisional (gates.json PROPOSED), exploration only: IS->OOS base profit per day: BTC -96%, ETH -63%, BNB -96%. Exploration cross-pair consistency (min/max profit per day) 0.22, below the 0.25 portfolio minimum. Mark-to-market drawdown 24%/25%/48% vs gate 14.0%/11.4%/9.7%. Source: research/audit/fase2-diagnostico.md.] [Frozen for dry-run evidence collection 2026-11-05T17:29:09.726808+00:00, commit 6d59a5711a, strategy sha256 456e194f571e; Dry-run como coleta de evidência: NÃO validada; sem evidência prospectiva; não é aprovação, não é holdout e não consome a leitura da validação.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-017','WeeklyBreakoutRegime','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance (same exposure rule as H-009). Identical to H-009 except for ONE added regime condition. REGIME at bar t: SMA(720)(t) > SMA(2160)(t) AND close(t) > SMA(720)(t) AND SMA(2160)(t) > SMA(2160)(t-720) (the 90-day mean is higher than it was 30 days ago, i.e. the slow trend is rising). ENTRY at close of bar t when REGIME holds AND close(t) > highest high of the prior 168 bars (t-168..t-1, excluding current bar) AND no open position AND cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t (executed next open) when close(t) < lowest low of the prior 72 bars (excluding current bar) OR close(t) < SMA(720)(t). STOP-LOSS: fixed 6% below entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 24 candles after any exit. No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters. The slope lag of 720 bars is fixed ex ante (30 days); no other value is run, the grid is the single cell {720}, with H-009 (no slope condition) as the reference. Warm-up: 2880 bars.','2026-11-04T13:36:02.214749+00:00','Context file research/context/H-017.md with exploration-only audit facts for H-009; no price data, validation or final test results were viewed.','rejected at exploration','Weekly breakout gated by a rising 90-day mean to avoid post-peak failed breakouts Calibrated exposure: 0.3 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.17130307434664505, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.24866607440735666, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.19669332877281875}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 54, ''ETH/USDT'': 70, ''BNB/USDT'': 62}. [Audit 2026-11-04, provisional (gates.json PROPOSED), exploration only: rejected at exploration. ETH failed the gate on max drawdown at the stress cost (25.5% > 25%) at the rule-calibrated exposure 0.3; BTC and BNB passed. Paired against H-009 on the same window and costs: daily-return correlation 0.86 (BTC) / 0.89 (ETH) / 0.98 (BNB); H-017 in-position time lies 100% inside H-009''s; base_2x Sharpe at exposure 0.3: 0.78 vs 1.12 (BTC), 0.54 vs 0.58 (ETH), 0.64 vs 0.61 (BNB); redundant. Longest losing streak fell (9->7, 14->11, 11->6) but the mark-to-market drawdown barely changed (H-017 12%/27%/34% vs H-009 at the same exposure 13%/29%/34%). Single-cell grid by design: DSR, PBO and plateau not computed. Validation not read. Source: research/audit/H-017-exploration-metrics.json, H-009x30-exploration-metrics.json. Archived.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-018','DonchianEnsemble','Protocol docs/protocolo-validacao-v3.md section 2.2. Signals come from CLOSED daily candles (merge_informative_pair, ffill, as in Sma200Baseline) and are executed on the 1h chart at the next open. Four members (N, M) = (20,10), (55,20), (100,50), (200,100). Member state is a two-level latch computed on the daily frame: ON when daily close > max(daily high of the N days before the current day) ; OFF when daily close < min(daily low of the M days before the current day) ; otherwise the previous state is kept ; undefined (NaN) channel values give OFF. Channels use rolling(N).max().shift(1) and rolling(M).min().shift(1) on the daily frame before the merge. ENTRY: at least 2 of the 4 members are ON and the strategy is flat (level entry, including the first candle of a split if already ON). EXIT: fewer than 2 members ON. No stop-loss (stoploss attribute -0.99 only to satisfy the engine contract), no take-profit, no sizing hooks, no cooldown. Exposure is the fixed share chosen by the lab rule (bootstrap.choose_exposure on exploration trades). Sensitivities reported, never selectable: threshold 1 and 3 of 4, each member alone, the vote without member (20,10), thresholds counted in the DSR N. Warm-up: 400 bars (daily candles; the state at the first day of a split was verified equal to the full-history state for 400, 600 and 900 days on BTC, ETH and BNB).','2026-11-04T18:26:46.153196+00:00','Protocol v3 and exploration-only audit facts; no validation or holdout result was used for this rule.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Donchian ensemble: majority vote of four daily channels, no stop. Protocol v3 (docs/protocolo-validacao-v3.md); decisions D-1..D-10 per the user''s 2026-11-04 ''use all proposals''; gates.json/portfolio.json still PROPOSED, so every decision is provisional. DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 17, ''ETH/USDT'': 14, ''BNB/USDT'': 16} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned. [Smoke, lookahead and recursive clean on BTC, ETH, BNB before the calibration. Result: inconclusive by the 30-trade rule (protocol D-2 kept); no gate decision, no validation read, no sensitivity run. Archived. Consequence: the Donchian family cannot be evaluated at daily horizons under the current gate; any change of the 30-trade rule is a user decision (D-2) and cannot be made after seeing this result for H-018.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-019','DailyRSI2Dip','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (Freqtrade informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no profit target, no sizing hooks. Indicators on daily closes: RSI(2) with Wilder smoothing (alpha = 1/2, seeded with the simple average of the first 2 changes); SMA(200 days); SMA(5 days). ENTRY when a daily candle closes with: daily close > SMA(200) AND RSI(2) < 10 AND no open position. EXIT when a daily candle closes with: daily close > SMA(5) OR daily close < SMA(200). STOP-LOSS: none in the rule (published exit only); the strategy sets stoploss = -0.99 only to satisfy the engine contract, never a binding stop. No cooldown. No other filters. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). All numbers fixed ex ante from the published rule: RSI length 2, threshold 10, exit average 5 days, trend average 200 days; no grid. Warm-up: 400 bars (daily candles on the informative frame: 200 for SMA(200) plus 200 for Wilder RSI to stabilise; the 1h startup_candle_count is set to 400 as in H-015/H-018, well under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-04T21:41:04.194059+00:00','No price data seen; only research/context/H-019.md exploration-level summaries and the protocol; BTC, ETH, BNB 1h through 2026-11-04 exist but were not inspected.','rejected at exploration','Daily RSI(2) oversold dip buy inside a 200-day uptrend, exit above 5-day SMA Calibrated exposure: 0.2 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.17410420469738616, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.21622252679628054, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.15089732849803617}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 53, ''ETH/USDT'': 54, ''BNB/USDT'': 57}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-020','Double7ChannelDip','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (Freqtrade informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no profit target, no time exit, no sizing hooks, no cooldown, no other filters. Indicators on daily closes: SMA(200 days) of daily close; lowest daily close of the last 7 days INCLUDING the current (just closed) day; highest daily close of the last 7 days INCLUDING the current day. ENTRY when a daily candle closes with: daily close > SMA(200) AND daily close <= lowest daily close of the last 7 days (including that day) AND no open position. EXIT when a daily candle closes with: daily close >= highest daily close of the last 7 days (including that day). STOP-LOSS: none in the published rule; the strategy sets stoploss = -0.99 only to satisfy the engine contract, never a binding stop. Lookbacks: 7 days entry channel, 7 days exit channel, 200 days trend filter; no grid, no tuning. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Warm-up: 400 bars (daily candles on the informative frame: 200 for the SMA(200) plus 200 spare; startup_candle_count 400 as in H-015/H-019, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T15:45:17.012151+00:00','No price data viewed; only the research context file (hypothesis list and exploration summaries) and the validation protocol; BTC, ETH, BNB 1h data not inspected.','exploration: candidate','Daily Double 7: buy a 7-day closing low above the 200-day mean, sell a 7-day closing high Calibrated exposure: 0.1 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.07103916095809959, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.21304422295439313, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.16275232274666154}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 58, ''ETH/USDT'': 66, ''BNB/USDT'': 64}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-021','DailyIBSDip','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (Freqtrade informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no profit target, no time exit, no sizing hooks, no other filters. Daily IBS = (close - low) / (high - low) of the closed daily candle; days with high == low are skipped (no signal, state unchanged). SMA200 = simple mean of the last 200 daily closes including the just-closed day. ENTRY when a daily candle closes with IBS < 0.2 AND daily close > SMA200 AND no open position. EXIT (first that occurs) when a later daily candle closes with IBS >= 0.8, OR a daily candle closes below SMA200 (safety exit), OR the hard stop. STOP-LOSS: one fixed 12% below the entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: none. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: IBS entry threshold 0.2, IBS exit threshold 0.8, trend mean 200 days, stop 12%. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Warm-up: 400 bars (daily candles on the informative frame: 200 for the SMA200 plus 200 spare; startup_candle_count 400 as in H-015/H-019/H-020, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T17:23:13.785085+00:00','No price data viewed; only the research context file with exploration-level summaries of earlier hypotheses (data up to 2026-11-05 not inspected).','failed: causality checks','Daily internal bar strength dip buy inside a 200-day uptrend');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-022','ThreeDayLowerRangeDip','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (Freqtrade informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no add-ons, no profit target, no time exit, no sizing hooks, no cooldown, no other filters. Indicators on daily data: SMA(200) of daily close and SMA(5) of daily close, both including the just-closed day. Let H(d), L(d) be the daily high and low of day d, d = the just-closed day. THREE-DAY FALLING RANGE: H(d)<H(d-1) AND L(d)<L(d-1) AND H(d-1)<H(d-2) AND L(d-1)<L(d-2) AND H(d-2)<H(d-3) AND L(d-2)<L(d-3) (strict inequalities). ENTRY when a daily candle closes with: close(d) > SMA200(d) AND close(d) < SMA5(d) AND the three-day falling range holds AND no open position. EXIT (first that occurs): a daily candle closes above SMA5; OR a daily candle closes below SMA200 (safety exit); OR the hard stop. STOP-LOSS: one fixed 12% below the entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: none. All numbers fixed ex ante from the published method, no grid: 200-day trend mean, 5-day exit/entry mean, 3 falling days, 12% stop. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Warm-up: 400 bars (daily candles on the informative frame: 200 for SMA(200) plus 200 spare; startup_candle_count 400 as in H-015/H-019/H-020/H-021, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T18:40:32.938103+00:00','No price data seen. Only research/context/H-022.md (exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses) and research/validation-protocol-v2.md; BTC, ETH, BNB 1h.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Connors 3-day lower highs and lows pullback inside a 200-day uptrend (daily signals, 1h execution) DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 25, ''ETH/USDT'': 31, ''BNB/USDT'': 32} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-023','DailyR3Streak','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (Freqtrade informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no profit target, no time exit, no sizing hooks, no cooldown, no other filters. Indicators on daily closes: RSI(2) with Wilder smoothing (alpha = 1/2, seeded with the simple average of the first 2 changes); SMA(200 days) including the just-closed day. Let RSI(0) be the RSI of the just-closed day d, RSI(1), RSI(2), RSI(3) the values 1, 2, 3 days earlier. ENTRY when a daily candle closes with: close(d) > SMA200(d) AND RSI(0) < RSI(1) AND RSI(1) < RSI(2) AND RSI(2) < RSI(3) (strict, three consecutive falls) AND RSI(3) < 60 AND RSI(0) < 10 AND no open position. EXIT when a daily candle closes with RSI(0) > 70. STOP-LOSS: none in the published rule; the strategy sets stoploss = -0.99 only to satisfy the engine contract, never a binding stop. No cooldown. All numbers fixed ex ante from the published rule, no grid: RSI length 2, entry threshold 10, prior-reading cap 60, exit threshold 70, 3 falling days, trend mean 200 days. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Warm-up: 400 bars (daily candles on the informative frame: 200 for SMA(200) plus 200 for the Wilder RSI to stabilise; the 1h startup_candle_count is set to 400 as in H-015/H-019/H-020, well under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T18:56:37.346980+00:00','No price data inspected; only the context file''s exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses (BTC, ETH, BNB 1h, exploration split) through 2026-11-05.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Daily R3: three falling RSI(2) days ending below 10 in a 200-day uptrend DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 18, ''ETH/USDT'': 20, ''BNB/USDT'': 22} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-001','S20261104T205946Z','Daily RSI(2) oversold dip buy in 200-day uptrend, exit above 5-day SMA','blog','https://therighttrader.com/learn/trading-strategies/rsi-2-strategy','RSI 2 Strategy (therighttrader.com)','unknown','Signals from closed DAILY candles built from the 1h data, executed at the next 1h open. RSI(2) uses Wilder smoothing on daily closes. ENTRY: daily close > SMA(200 days) of daily close AND RSI(2) < 10 AND no open position. EXIT: first daily close above SMA(5 days) of daily close, OR daily close below SMA(200 days). No profit target, no pyramiding. Optional protective stop (not part of the published exit): none in the base rule; a developer may add a fixed percentage stop below entry. Free numbers: RSI length 2, threshold 10, exit average 5, trend average 200.','Very short-term sell-offs inside an established uptrend are often forced or impatient selling (liquidations, panic sellers) that overshoots; liquidity takers pay a concession to dip buyers, and price snaps back toward its short mean. The source gives only a brief rationale (extreme readings flag dips; the 200-day filter avoids downtrends); the liquidity-overshoot story is the closest honest mechanism.','1d',200,4,1,9.0,'DailyRSI2Dip','89cdd0d318c9fa83fc961babbf54823dd6a77b3395b6d4a6aca0d21b74512381','registered','formalised as H-019',2.9379,'H-019','2026-11-04T21:00:41.983635+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-002','S20261105T154404Z','Daily Double 7: buy a 7-day closing low above the 200-day mean, sell a 7-day closing high','blog','https://strategyquant.com/blog/larry-connors-double-7-strategy-tested-on-spy-and-8-other-markets/','Larry Connors'' Double 7 Strategy: Tested on SPY and 8 Other Markets','unknown','Daily signals from closed daily candles built from the 1h data; orders executed at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole balance. ENTRY when a daily close is above the 200-day simple moving average of daily closes AND that close is less than or equal to the lowest daily close of the last 7 days (including the current day) AND no position is open. EXIT when a daily close is greater than or equal to the highest daily close of the last 7 days (including the current day). No stop, no profit target, no time exit. Lookbacks: 7 days for entry channel, 7 days for exit channel, 200 days for the trend filter.','Counterparty: short-horizon sellers who capitulate or de-risk after a few down days inside a long-term uptrend, pushing price below fair value for a short time; liquidity-demanding panic sellers pay a premium to exit. Short-term reversal after a pullback is paid to the buyer who supplies liquidity. The source gives no mechanism beyond the stock-index mean reversion observation; this is the closest honest one.','1d',200,3,1,9.0,'Double7ChannelDip','f0f19b8980a768896d77b527e47b9400160e7b68404b216f53ba76ccf5891bcf','registered','formalised as H-020',3.3251,'H-020','2026-11-05T15:44:47.191227+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-003','S20261105T172127Z','Daily internal bar strength dip buy in 200-day uptrend','repo','https://doc.stocksharp.com/en/api-examples/0927_Internal_Bar_Strength_IBS','Internal Bar Strength IBS Strategy (StockSharp docs)','unknown','Daily signals from closed UTC daily candles built from 1h data, executed at the next 1h open. IBS = (close - low) / (high - low) of the daily candle; skip days with zero range. ENTRY when a daily candle closes with IBS < 0.2 AND daily close > SMA(200 days) AND no open position. EXIT when a later daily candle closes with IBS >= 0.8. Safety exit: daily close below the 200-day SMA. Optional hard stop 12% below entry. Long only, one position per pair, whole balance. The source uses 0.2 and 0.8 thresholds on 4h bars with no trend filter; the 200-day filter and daily frame are my adaptation.','A close near the day''s low in an uptrend often reflects forced selling or liquidity-driven pressure at the end of the day. Dip buyers who provide liquidity are paid when price reverts the next sessions. The source gives no mechanism; this is the usual short-term reversal / liquidity-provision explanation.','1d',200,4,1,14.0,'DailyIBSDip','665ca9337a26f817ae3886f1d35a3643611d21f22d9a804bd196a0b8eec4e1be','registered','formalised as H-021',3.1905,'H-021','2026-11-05T17:22:20.894055+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-004','S20261105T172127Z','Connors 3-day lower highs and lows pullback in 200-day uptrend','blog','https://www.tradingview.com/script/2DMs2jT9','Larry Connors 3-day high/low method (TradingView open-source script)','unknown','Daily signals from closed UTC daily candles built from 1h data, executed at the next 1h open. ENTRY when a daily candle closes with: close > SMA(200 days); close < SMA(5 days); and three consecutive days of falling range, meaning each of the last three daily candles has both a lower high and a lower low than the candle before it (today vs yesterday, yesterday vs two days ago, two days ago vs three days ago); and no open position. EXIT when a daily close is above SMA(5 days). Safety exit: daily close below SMA(200 days) or 12% below entry. Long only, one position per pair, whole balance, no add-ons (the source''s optional add-on is excluded).','Three successive days of lower highs and lows inside a long-term uptrend is a short-lived selling streak. Impatient sellers and stop-triggered holders push price below its short mean, and buyers who provide liquidity are paid when price snaps back to the 5-day mean. The source states no mechanism; this is the standard short-term reversal explanation.','1d',200,4,1,8.0,'ThreeDayLowerRangeDip','57b1f8d970a707f77122887507d9d8c89b89aa3f4c65bdc7c1faea6abfa43a1f','registered','formalised as H-022',2.5137,'H-022','2026-11-05T17:22:20.900770+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-005','S20261105T183908Z','Daily R3: three falling RSI(2) readings ending below 10, in 200-day uptrend','repo','https://in.tradingview.com/script/5CDSns2I-R3-ETF-Strategy','R3 ETF Strategy (TradingView open-source script, after Connors and Alvarez)','unknown','All signals from closed daily candles (UTC) built from 1h data, executed at next 1h open. Compute RSI(2) on daily closes and SMA(200 days) of daily close. ENTRY when a daily candle closes with: close > SMA200 AND RSI(2) has fallen on each of the last three days (RSI today < RSI yesterday < RSI two days ago < RSI three days ago) AND RSI(2) three days ago was below 60 AND RSI(2) today is below 10, with no open position. EXIT when a daily close has RSI(2) above 70. No stop, no profit target. One position per pair, whole balance.','A multi-day one-way slide that ends in extreme short-term oversold inside a long-term uptrend is typically forced or panicked selling (liquidations, stop runs). Liquidity providers and dip buyers on the other side collect the usual partial snap-back. The source gives no mechanism beyond the ETF mean-reversion claim; this is the closest honest one.','1d',200,5,1,7.0,'DailyR3Streak','ab7bf7d7a72fee656de5e0d908a5b8774dca7b80618d1c014fb646352f63974c','registered','formalised as H-023',2.2501,'H-023','2026-11-05T18:39:53.248450+00:00');
